// shader-differential - texture WRAP control, sampled side (2026-09-02).
//
// Samples u_tex at TEXCOORD1.xy = (u - 0.5, v - 0.5), a coordinate window
// that is half outside 0..1 on each axis - the window th06's shaders use
// (`float4 uv : TEXCOORD1`).  Under CLAMP_TO_EDGE that window read texels
// 0..31 only, and tex0's permuted alpha ramp never dropped below 0.5
// there, so four of the nine corpus discard witnesses (th06_probe_alpha,
// probe_mulrgb, probe_texrgb, th06_rep: `t.a < 4/255`) read discard-blind
// on the reference side.  The rig now addresses every texture WRAP, so a
// 1.0-wide window traverses every ramp wherever it sits; this row is the
// proof that wrapped sampling lands on the texel the arithmetic twin
// predicts (sd_tex_wrap_baked.fcg, frac-based).  Same role as the plain
// texture control: a mismatch here withholds every sampler-declaring
// verdict.  Proven to fire by booting the CLAMP guest against this
// manifest (the row must go red there).
void main(
    float4 in_texcoord1  : TEXCOORD1,
    uniform sampler2D u_tex : TEXUNIT0,
    out float4 out_color : COLOR)
{
    out_color = tex2D(u_tex, in_texcoord1.xy);
}
